**Your mission**
----------------

Thanks to your sense of leadership and planning skills, you will be responsible for the organization and management of all activities related to the smooth operation of the distribution centre.

“The Distribution Centre Manager is dynamic, possesses a business manager’s clarity of vision and loves to work in a team. A strong leader who brings people together, drives performance, and turns operational challenges into opportunities for success.” Nicolas Charbonneau, Vice-President of Operations.

**What you’d mainly be responsible for:**
-----------------------------------------

* Planning, organizing, coordinating, supervising and controlling day and evening operations related to order shipping and receiving;
* Motivating and effectively managing staff;
* Participating in employee recruitment, training, evaluation and also monitoring individual performance, continuous improvement of productivity and the quality of work of the entire team;
* Establishing effective communications with your employees and maintaining an excellent work climate while respecting the application of the current collective agreement and ensuring employee compliance with the relevant standards and policies;
* Following up on complaints concerning the distribution centre in collaboration with Customer Service and implementing corrective measures;
* Acting as the primary point of contact for all our local transport service providers and our Customer Service team and working with our carriers to maximize the client experience while meeting our budget objectives;
* Taking necessary measures to minimize health and safety hazards for employees and visitors and ensuring the proper use of material and equipment by employees;
* Recommending changes to work methods and the use of human and material resources in order to optimize the quality, service and/or profitability of the company;
* Identifying the equipment and manpower needs required for the proper functioning of your department, participating in the preparation of operating budgets and staying within those budgets;
* Establishing an impeccable work environment;
* Ensuring the application of good manufacturing practices;
* Overseeing the maintenance of the distribution centre’s premises and equipment;
* Maintaining healthy working relationships;
* Performing any other task required by your supervisor to best serve the interests of CDMV.

**Does this describe you?**
---------------------------

* Minimum of 3 years of experience in a similar position;
* Experience in team supervision and employee training;
* Good experience working with warehouse management systems (WMS’s and ERP).

**Does this sound like you?**
-----------------------------

* Adaptability and good organizational skills;
* Rigour and reliability;
* Vision and vigilance in matters of occupational health and safety;
* Mastery of basic principles of warehouse management;
* Autonomous, good sense of urgency and resourceful;
* Ability to unite and motivate others;
* Sense of leadership.

**We have a lot to offer:**
---------------------------

* Competitive pension plan.
* Group insurance including life, disability and dental insurance.
* Employee and family assistance programs (EFAP).
* Onboarding and integration program.
* Talent management program.
* A company that promotes career advancement.

CDMV is the leading Canada-wide distributor of products for veterinary practices.

We have been supporting veterinarians and their teams by offering them a wide range of quality products since 1972.

We honour our mission by striving for consistent operational excellence in all our distribution centres located in Alberta, Quebec and Nova Scotia.

By joining CDMV, you’ll become part a team of over 300 employees who care deeply about the health and well-being of animals.

